    {
      "type": "deb",
      "namespace": "debian",
      "name": "libhogweed6t64",
      "version": "3.10.1-1",
      "purl": "pkg:deb/debian/libhogweed6t64@3.10.1-1?arch=amd64&os_distro=trixie&os_name=debian&os_version=13&upstream=nettle",
      "author": "Magnus Holmgren <holmgren@debian.org>",
      "description": "low level cryptographic library (public-key cryptos)\n Nettle is a cryptographic library that is designed to fit easily in more or\n less any context: In crypto toolkits for object-oriented languages (C++,\n Python, Pike, ...), in applications like LSH or GNUPG, or even in kernel\n space.\n .\n It tries to solve a problem of providing a common set of cryptographic\n algorithms for higher-level applications by implementing a\n context-independent set of cryptographic algorithms. In that light, Nettle\n doesn't do any memory allocation or I/O, it simply provides the\n cryptographic algorithms for the application to use in any environment and\n in any way it needs.\n .\n This package contains the asymmetric cryptographic algorithms, which,\n require the GNU multiple precision arithmetic library (libgmp) for\n their large integer computations.",
      "licenses": [
        "GPL-2.0-only",
        "GPL-2.0-or-later",
        "GPL-3.0-or-later",
        "LGPL-2.0-only",
        "LGPL-2.0-or-later",
        "LGPL-3.0-or-later"
      ],
      "installed_size": 483,
      "locations": [
